            <chunk name="Object" index="22">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">37999bc8-757c-4c9e-a0ed-adb337fbbba5</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">FACADE PRESSURE
Wind-driven facade Cp, and the EnergyPlus
AirflowNetwork hand-off. Units: METERS.

CHAIN
Outdoor Case &gt; Buildings (the meshed geometry)
  -&gt; Facade Grid    1 m spacing, 0.05 m offset,
     Max Tilt 45 so only near-vertical faces
     count as facade (90 would include roofs and
     ground). Flip off.
  -&gt; Probe          Field "Cp", at those points,
     on the solved case
  -&gt; Airflow Network Cp
     writes a WindPressureCoefficientArray, per
     node WindPressureCoefficientValues and
     ExternalNode objects as an .idf snippet to
     merge into a Ladybug Tools AirflowNetwork
     model. Ground Z 0. Write ships OFF and the
     File Path is empty, so opening this document
     cannot write a file.
The ABL component's Boundary Conditions feed
Airflow Network Cp so the exported array carries
the simulated wind directions.

FACADE WIND PRESSURE sits alongside as the
analytic EN 1991-1-4 cross-check: basic wind
25 m/s, opening at 10 m on a 20 x 40 m building,
zone D (windward), terrain 3 (suburban). It is
NOT wired into the CFD chain - it is the
code-based number you compare the simulated Cp
against.

*** TWO THINGS TO KNOW ***
1. Probe and Airflow Network Cp show warnings
   until the case is solved. That is the
   unsolved state, not a wiring fault: this
   template deliberately ships no cached results.
2. Airflow Network Cp's own help says "Enable
   Pressure Coefficient in Run Settings". On the
   installed 1.9.0.827 Run Settings has no such
   input - it is not in the component's parameter
   list. Until it appears, the Cp field has to
   come from whatever your build writes; check
   the case's function objects before probing.

Nothing in the shipped catalog used Facade Grid,
Facade Wind Pressure or Airflow Network Cp before
this template.

Action toggles ship OFF.</item>
                  </items>
