                    <chunk name="param_input" index="7">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Numerics as a point on the Accuracy / Robustness / Speed triangle. It sets the convection and gradient schemes, the under-relaxation, the non-orthogonal correctors, the laplacian correction (unless Laplacian Scheme overrides it), the linear-solver relTol and the auto warm-up length together. Accuracy corner: second-order convection, high relaxation, full laplacian correction — captures wakes and eddies but needs a good mesh and warms up first. Robustness corner: first-order upwind, heavy relaxation, three correctors — always converges, smears wakes by numerical diffusion. Speed corner: first-order upwind, one corrector, loose relTol, short warm-up. The old 1-5 levels are named points (right-click, or the picker's buttons); the default is level 4, the shipped baseline, so nothing changes until the dot moves. Accepts a wired "4" or "a,r,s". Standards note: the ASCE/SEI CWE Prestandard's AC 4-3 needs second-order convection — the Accuracy side (levels 1-3); the Robustness/Speed side is first-order upwind.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">0bdb4f52-a2d3-44d8-92e0-139ba436453a</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Numerics</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Num</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="Value" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">0.5,0.5,0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="2">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>395</X>
                              <Y>1487</Y>
                              <W>53</W>
                              <H>20</H>
                            </item>
                            <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                              <X>423</X>
                              <Y>1497</Y>
                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                        <chunk name="PersistentData">
                          <items count="1">
                            <item name="Count" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                          </items>
                          <chunks count="1">
                            <chunk name="Branch" index="0">
                              <items count="2">
                                <item name="Count" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
