                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Wind-driven facade pressure coefficients for building energy modelling, across eight wind directions. Atmospheric Boundary Layer takes directions from Series (0 to 315 degrees, 45 degree steps); Outdoor Case sets up two 40 x 20 x 20 m blocks in a Cylinder Domain, and Run Settings enables Cp output. Facade Grid places points at 1 m spacing, 0.05 m offset, on faces within 45 degrees of vertical. Probe reads Cp there (set Field to Cp), and Airflow Network Cp writes an EnergyPlus AirflowNetwork .idf snippet for Ladybug Tools. Probe warns until the case is solved. Replace the blocks with your building.</item>
                  </items>
